# Laravel's scheduler (plan §5.5, §10).
#
# Everything time-based in EzBizi hangs off this: audit retention, closing
# expired impersonation sessions, and — since the automation engine landed —
# draining the outbox. Without it the whole automation subsystem is decorative:
# events pile up in automation_events, nothing is ever delivered, and no error is
# raised anywhere because nothing is broken. It simply never runs.
#
# A systemd timer rather than a crontab line, so failures land in the journal
# alongside everything else instead of in root's mail spool.
#
# Points at the CURRENT symlink, not a release directory, so a deploy swaps the
# code underneath it without touching this unit.
#
# A TEMPLATE, started by three timers (ezbizi-scheduler-0/1/2.timer) on
# staggered minutes, so up to three runs can overlap. One oneshot unit on one
# every-minute timer could not: systemd does not start a unit that is still
# running, and schedule:run evaluates only the minute it STARTS in. With runs
# of 75-100 s (sync-leads, sync-workiz, project-workiz, measured 2026-10-06),
# 15-32 minutes of every hour were never evaluated, and whatever was pinned to
# them (hourly sync-workiz-team, daily expire-data, warn-overbooking) silently
# did not run. Each instance now has three minutes. Every per-minute command
# in routes/console.php carries withoutOverlapping, so overlapping runs skip
# what is still running rather than doubling it.
# ponytail: three slots; a run past 180 s skips again. Add a fourth timer
# (OnCalendar=*:N/4 on each) if runs grow that long.
#
# Install:
#   sudo cp deploy/ezbizi-scheduler@.service deploy/ezbizi-scheduler-[012].timer /etc/systemd/system/
#   sudo systemctl daemon-reload
#   sudo systemctl enable --now ezbizi-scheduler-0.timer ezbizi-scheduler-1.timer ezbizi-scheduler-2.timer

[Unit]
Description=EzBizi scheduled tasks (slot %i)
After=network.target mysql.service
OnFailure=ezbizi-scheduler-failed@%N.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=www-data
Group=www-data
WorkingDirectory=/var/www/ezbizi-current
ExecStart=/usr/bin/php8.4 /var/www/ezbizi-current/artisan schedule:run

# A scheduled task that hangs must not hold the next minute's run hostage.
TimeoutStartSec=300

# The app needs storage/ and bootstrap/cache; nothing else on the box.
PrivateTmp=true
NoNewPrivileges=true
ProtectSystem=full
ProtectHome=true
